 "dur": 45.442,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Big Hank's brakes glowed like toasters, and he waved off the ramp.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.125
  },
  {
   "text": "Behind him, forty tons of watermelons. Beside him, Pickles the pig, drooling.",
   "s": 3.325,
   "e": 7.061
  },
  {
   "text": "\"No sandbox for Hank!\" he told Junie, his rookie, as the gravel ramp flew by.",
   "s": 7.261,
   "e": 11.477
  },
  {
   "text": "He'd ridden the brakes for eleven miles: warm, toasty, glowing, smoking.",
   "s": 11.677,
   "e": 14.955
  },
  {
   "text": "So he poured his coffee on them. Now they were glowing and steaming.",
   "s": 15.155,
   "e": 18.069
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the pedal sank to the floor like a whoopee cushion. Forty tons, no brakes.",
   "s": 18.269,
   "e": 21.845
  },
  {
   "text": "But one ramp was left before Main Street. \"No sandbox for Hank!\"",
   "s": 22.045,
   "e": 25.171
  },
  {
   "text": "Why would brakes that worked at the top quit at the bottom?",
   "s": 25.291,
   "e": 27.503
  },
  {
   "text": "Brakes stop a truck by rubbing, and rubbing makes heat. Eleven miles of heat.",
   "s": 27.803,
   "e": 31.32
  },
  {
   "text": "Too hot, and they turn slippery, like grabbing a wet bar of soap.",
   "s": 31.72,
   "e": 34.777
  },
  {
   "text": "So Junie yanked the wheel, straight into the sandbox.",
   "s": 34.977,
   "e": 37.218
  },
  {
   "text": "Deep loose gravel swallows the wheels and soaks up the speed, like a ball pit.",
   "s": 37.419,
   "e": 40.847
  },
  {
   "text": "Hank got his first sandbox. Pickles got forty tons of melon.",
   "s": 41.047,
   "e": 44.142
  }
 ],
